Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
Social Security Numbers (SSNs) do not have expiry dates. 

If you are applying for a six-month visa, the expiry date requirement almost certainly refers to your **passport**. Most countries require that your passport remains valid for at least six months beyond your intended date of departure from their country. 

If you can provide the expiry date of your passport and your intended travel dates, I can help you figure out if it is valid for your visa application!

